// FIELD SERVICE — HARVEST — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// FIELD SERVICE as folk-house — a game alternate of plumber, selectable from the dev
// menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// The countryside cabinet's song gone to the barn dance: the hook on a plucked koto
// over stomp, clap, tambourine and a strummed chord, then a four-on-the-floor drop —
// pumping supersaw chords, an off-beat bass, the hook on a mega-saw lead. The
// breakdown hands the tune to an ocarina whistle; the second drop keeps the whistle
// and, in its second half, adds plumber.js's own harmony line (leadHarm) on a flute.
// 
//   1–4    intro — koto hook, strum, stomp and shaker (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–12   verse — stomp-clap and tambourine, A A B B
//   13–16  build — F, G, Esus4, E; claps to eighths, snare roll, riser
//   17–32  drop — four on the floor, supersaw pump, A A B B A A C C
//   33–40  breakdown — ocarina, strum and grand; C then A phrase at half speed
//   41–44  build — again, harder
//   45–60  drop two — the whistle doubles the hook, then the harmony joins
//   61–64  outro — koto and stomp; the loop returns to bar 5
// 
